The {{nihongo|'''Nanboku Line'''|南北線|Nanboku-sen}} is a subway line in [[Okami|Okami (大紙)]], [[Okaiken]], operated by [[Okami Metro]]. True to its name (''Nanboku'' means "South-North"), it serves as a critical vertical spine for the city, running parallel to the older [[Miyoshi Line]] to relieve congestion. On system maps, the line is color-coded blue ({{Okami Metro color|B}}) and its stations use the prefix "B".

===Connectivity and Operations===
The Nanboku Line is unique among Okami subways as it utilizes an overhead catenary system (1500 V DC) instead of the standard third rail. This allows for extensive through-services with private railways at both termini.
* Northern Terminus: At [[Higashi-Tatara Station|Higashi-Tatara (B01)]], the line connects to the [[Akitetsu|Akitetsu Akita Main Line]], extending service north into the mountainous suburbs.
* Southern Terminus: At [[Yanagihama Station|Yanagihama (B22)]], trains continue onto the [[Tokutetsu|Tokutetsu Nada Line]] toward [[Aono Station|Aono]].

The line supports three service types:
* Local: Stops at all stations.
* Rapid: Skips minor stops between major transfer hubs.
* Limited Express "Akitoku" (秋徳): A premium commuter liner that runs from Akita (via Akitetsu) to Tokuyama, utilizing the Nanboku Line's high-speed underground straightaways.

